// shelf.templ — Zone D, the foot of the Block, and FILLED.
//
// WAVE 2 FILLS IT (C-CALV4-SHELF-P7, W-E). Wave 1 docked the zone at its real
// size carrying the signed `needs backend` chip, GATED on ShelfStub.NeedsBackend
// specifically so the chip could retire by a producer flag rather than a
// template edit — the promise the flag existed to keep, now kept.
//
// data-zone="shelf" SURVIVES VERBATIM on the outer div. seamLayerSurfaces
// (block_seam_test.go) keys TestSeam_EnabledLayerSetMatchesWhatRenders on that
// exact marker: rename the file, replace the body, keep the marker — or the
// test goes green while proving nothing.
//
// GEOMETRY IS INVARIANT AND LOAD-BEARING. `.st` is 34px, `.sp2` is 132px with
// its own scroller. The Block's declared heights depend on it. The body
// scrolls; the zone does not grow.
//
// The Shelf honours ShelfStub.Hidden — the Bench's real-world Block renders with
// noShelf, and a hidden Shelf must actually REMOVE the zone rather than collapse
// it, or the Block's declared heights stop being invariant. The removal is the
// CALL SITE's (block.templ), which is why that condition is written there and
// not here; this comment is carried forward because it is the reason the branch
// exists at all.
//
// THE SHELF READS. Contract §8 item 2 (L5): the celestial surface is "a
// dedicated filtered Almanac list in the shelf widget — no fifth authoring
// surface". Nothing in this zone authors, and nothing in it configures itself
// ([S3]: "owner/scribe-configurable" is struck for wave 2 and re-booked to the
// wave that ships a config store).
//
// THREE DIVERGENCES FROM THE SIGNED FULL-TIER RENDERS, ALL PRE-AUTHORISED ([S8]):
//
//   - NO `sky: graph | words | moons | off` PICKER in the strip. It appears in
//     v4-sky-almanac-month.png and v4-sky-almanac-moons.png and has no emitter
//     anywhere in the signed HTML; those stills are round-7/8 output and design
//     notes L29 (round 11) settles it — "the second menu is gone … the
//     switchboard is now the only place layers are chosen".
//   - NO `filters N` BADGE ([S4]). With no filter engine it is a number with
//     nothing behind it, which is the exact shape the sync-pill ruling forbids
//     and the shape `needs backend` exists to replace. It returns WITH the
//     engine, and joins the per-viewer count oracle at that point.
//   - NO `Shelf` CAPTION. The signed strip carries its tabs and nothing else;
//     the caption was wave 1's way of naming a zone that had no content to name
//     itself. The tabs name it now.

package calendar_block

// shelf is Zone D.
//
// DOM ORDER IS THE SIGNED ORDER (cv4:1774-1801): the strip, then the body.
// Inside the strip the tabs, then the spacer. Inside the body: one panel per
// tab, all rendered, one revealed by the stylesheet.
//
// EVERY PANEL IS RENDERED ON EVERY RENDER and hidden by CSS, for the same
// reason the Ledger renders every day's head line: there is no JS in this
// package and no route to fetch a panel with, so the only thing a tab can do is
// change which already-rendered panel is displayed.
templ shelf(d BlockData) {
	<div class="shelf" data-zone="shelf">
		<div class="st" role="group" aria-label="Shelf panels">
			@shelfTab(d, shelfTabUpcoming, "Upcoming")
			if shelfShowsFilters(d) {
				@shelfTab(d, shelfTabFilters, "Filters")
			}
			if almanacReachable(d) {
				@shelfTab(d, shelfTabAlmanac, "Almanac")
				@almanacSubTabs(d)
			}
			<span class="sp"></span>
		</div>
		<div class="sp2">
			@shelfUpcomingPanel(d)
			if shelfShowsFilters(d) {
				@shelfFiltersPanel()
			}
			if almanacReachable(d) {
				@almanacPanel(d)
			}
		</div>
	</div>
}

// shelfTab is one tab: a visually-hidden radio plus its label.
//
// IT IS A RADIO AND NOT A BUTTON, and that is the whole mechanism ([S7],
// SIGNED). The state has to survive with no JS and no route, so it is the same
// shape the tie toggle proved and the day pick reuses: `display:none` would
// drop the input from the tab order AND from `:checked`, so it is zero-size and
// transparent instead, and the label borrows its focus ring.
//
// data-shelf-pick, not data-shelf: guard B3 — an interactive control never
// reuses an <html> state-marker noun, and controls end in `-pick`.
//
// NO TRAVELLING INDICATOR (canon A6): the pressed look is state ON the pressed
// item, never a thumb that slides between items.
templ shelfTab(d BlockData, key string, label string) {
	<input
		type="radio"
		class="shelfpick"
		data-shelf-pick={ key }
		name={ shelfPickGroupName(d) }
		id={ shelfPickInputID(d, key) }
		checked?={ shelfDefaultTab(d) == key }
	/>
	<label class="stab" for={ shelfPickInputID(d, key) }>{ label }</label>
}

// shelfUpcomingPanel is the signed Upcoming body (cv4:1793-1799).
//
// TWO BANDS AND THE LEDGER'S OWN ROW. `.lband` is Zone C vocabulary, styled by
// W-B and consumed here — the Ledger itself is flat and ungrouped, and shipping
// the band there rather than making this file redefine it is what keeps one
// vocabulary across the two zones.
//
// The rows are ledgerRow, VERBATIM. Not adapted, not re-cut: the Shelf's row
// primitive IS the Ledger's row primitive, so every row carries the same
// data-day ANSWER key (guard B4), the same gold-rail/audience split and the
// same tie-scoped ink, and the two zones cannot drift.
templ shelfUpcomingPanel(d BlockData) {
	{{ v := newShelfUpcoming(d) }}
	<div class="spane spane-upcoming" data-spane="upcoming">
		<div class="lband">Today</div>
		if len(v.Today) == 0 {
			<div class="lzero">{ shelfTodayZero(d, v) }</div>
		}
		for _, l := range v.Today {
			@ledgerRow(d, l)
		}
		<div class="lband">This month</div>
		if len(v.Later) == 0 {
			<div class="lzero">{ shelfLaterZero(d) }</div>
		}
		for _, l := range v.Later {
			@ledgerRow(d, l)
		}
		if v.Truncated {
			<div class="smore">{ shelfMoreText() }</div>
		}
	</div>
}

// shelfFiltersPanel is the Filters body, and it is one chip.
//
// [S2], SIGNED: THE TAB SHIPS AND THE ENGINE DOES NOT.
//
// HALF OF THIS BLOCKER IS NOW FALSE, AND THE SENTENCE IS REWRITTEN RATHER THAN
// DELETED. W-E wrote here that "no preference store of any kind exists in the
// repo … the same gap that keeps LayerState.HasSwitchboard false", and it was
// exactly right at the time. C-CALV4-LAYERS-P9 (W-F) built that store: calendar
// migration 014's block_layers column on calendar_active, POST
// /campaigns/:id/calendar/prefs, and a live switchboard. HasSwitchboard is true.
//
// WHAT IS STILL MISSING IS THE ENGINE, not the store. There is still no filter
// state on BlockData, no filter query anywhere in the plugin, and no
// ViewerContext.Filters pin field — the amendment refused one by name, because
// golangci's `unused` turns a field added ahead of its consumer into a red
// build. So: no filter controls, no inert chips, no fabricated state, and no
// pin field. The unconditional chip inside an enabled layer is still the honest
// state, exactly as the 2026-07-28 DEF/zone-chip ruling §2 sanctions.
//
// THE FILLING SLICE IS NAMED: C-CALV4-FILTERS-P10. Filter axes are per-viewer
// display preferences by the same argument that made the colour-by axis W-F's,
// and the store they need is designed to grow one more COLUMN rather than one
// more table. The `filters N` badge stays withheld ([S4]) until the engine
// ships and joins the count oracle with it.
//
// The panel renders for a GM only, because a `needs backend` chip never renders
// to a player (decisions/2026-07-27-needs-backend-audience.md) — and a player
// gets no Filters TAB either, so the tab never opens on nothing ([S10]).
templ shelfFiltersPanel() {
	<div class="spane spane-filters" data-spane="filters">
		<span class="badge need">needs backend</span>
		<span class="sneed">Filter axes need an engine; the per-viewer store is built.</span>
	</div>
}
